From: DrummingBird1 <1979036+DrummingBird1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:03:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vblank ticker: GCM_TICK_MS sets the walker's idle wait

The ticker waits up to 4 ms for a kick before draining the FIFO again,
and only a dry fence poll kicks it. A title that waits for the RSX in a
usleep loop or on a label never kicks, so its new commands sat for up to
4 ms on every hand-off. GCM_TICK_MS=<n> makes the wait configurable; the
default stays 4. Sonic 06's first scene: 25.8 flips/s at 4 ms, 28.4 at
1 ms, over 5 alternating pairs with the same exe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp b/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp
index e20ae428..7635ec4f 100644
--- a/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp
+++ b/runtime/ppu/tests/boot_main.cpp
@@ -497,7 +497,13 @@ static DWORD WINAPI vblank_ticker(LPVOID)
          * fence still paid the whole tick. Waiting on it keeps the same 4 ms
          * ceiling when nothing kicks, and drains on demand when something
          * does. */
-        cellGcm_fifo_kick_wait(4);
+        /* GCM_TICK_MS=<n>: the idle wait, for measuring how much of a frame
+         * is the walker noticing new commands late (only a dry fence poll
+         * kicks it; a title waiting in usleep or on a label does not). */
+        static int s_tick_ms = -1;
+        if (s_tick_ms < 0) { const char* e = getenv("GCM_TICK_MS"); s_tick_ms = e ? atoi(e) : 4;
+                             if (s_tick_ms < 0) s_tick_ms = 4; }
+        cellGcm_fifo_kick_wait((unsigned)s_tick_ms);
         unsigned long long now = ps3_qpc_us();
         int fired = 0;
         while (now >= tick_t0 + tick_k * 1000000ull / 60 && fired < 240) {
